{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794381653819,"sessionID":"ses_e36ac0041ffeAjsRq7kwpL3mQR","part":{"id":"prt_1c97b271a001lEatPpZKyzODet","messageID":"msg_1c97acb05001vhtUlcIcVkTJQs","sessionID":"ses_e36ac0041ffeAjsRq7kwpL3mQR","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794381653819,"sessionID":"ses_e36ac0041ffeAjsRq7kwpL3mQR","part":{"id":"prt_1c97b27220010JpJvgYgJVZxK3","messageID":"msg_1c97acb05001vhtUlcIcVkTJQs","sessionID":"ses_e36ac0041ffeAjsRq7kwpL3mQR","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a full shop app in `/workspace`: Flask JSON API under `/api` (auth, products, user carts with server-computed totals, admin product management) plus a React/TypeScript/Vite frontend styled with Tailwind, served by the same backend on port 8000 with SQLite under `./data`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Stack: Flask + gunicorn (Python 3.13), React 19 + TS + Vite 8, Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`, entry CSS is only `@import \"tailwindcss\";`).\n- Docker image: `npm ci` + `npm run build` for frontend; `pip install -r backend/requirements.lock` (I changed Dockerfile from `-r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` — that combination fails with pip 25.1.1: \"Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode\"; installing lock directly works). README updated to match.\n- `ADMIN_PASSWORD` env read at startup: set → admin user upserted (password hash updated, admin tokens deleted); unset/empty → admin login disabled (\"Admin sign-in is disabled\", 401) and admin tokens/password neutralized. Username \"admin\" is reserved (register → 400).\n- Money stored as integer `price_cents`; serialized as `price_cents/100`; line_total/subtotal computed in cents (exact integer math).\n- Error format: `{\"message\": ...}`; statuses: register 201/409/400, login 200 `{\"token\"}`/401, cart mutations 200 returning full cart, no token 401, other user's cart item 404, non-admin admin-route 403 (401 without token), inactive/missing product 404, invalid bodies 400.\n- Extra endpoints beyond spec: `GET /api/auth/me` → `{\"username\", \"is_admin\"}` (used by frontend session restore); frontend treats `isAdmin` from this.\n- Products: active only, `ORDER BY name COLLATE NOCASE, id`; defaults page=1, page_size=10 (max 100); `q` searches name+description case-insensitively with LIKE escaping; response `{items,total,page,page_size}`.\n- Cart: items ordered by `ci.id ASC` (oldest first); inactive products excluded from items and subtotal; adding never changes stock; quantity must be int ≥ 1 (0/negative → 400); no stock enforcement.\n- Seed: 9 products, each stock ≥ 10, inserted only when products table empty.\n- Cart badge shows total quantity (`sum of item.quantity`) — chosen interpretation of \"number of items\".\n- Add-to-cart button should stay enabled when signed out → opens auth modal (pending change; `canAdd` prop currently disables it — being removed).\n- Sandbox quirks: no docker; only `/workspace` and (partially) `/tmp/opencode/*` writable via tools — `/tmp/opencode` is root-owned so unusable; temp venv at `/tmp/venvA`; avoid `pkill -f ...gunicorn` (self-matches shell cmdline — use `pkill -x gunicorn`); start server with `setsid nohup ... < /dev/null &` or shell times out; `/dev/null` in commands may be blocked by permission rules.\n- Gunicorn run command: `setsid nohup env ADMIN_PASSWORD=secretpw /tmp/venvA/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath /workspace/backend app:app > /tmp/gunicorn.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &` (workdir `/workspace`).\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- `backend/app.py`: full API implemented (register/login/me, products list/get, cart GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE, admin POST/PATCH products, health, frontend serving with `/api/*` JSON 404 fallback, path-traversal-safe static serving).\n- Fixed `init_db()` crash: connection now has `conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row` (previously `row[\"id\"]` failed in `init_admin` when admin already existed — \"TypeError: tuple indices must be integers or slices, not str\").\n- Frontend fully written: auth modal (sign in/register tabs), header with username + sign-out + cart badge, product grid with placeholder tile, \"Out of stock\" badge, search (300ms debounce, page_size 12), paging, cart drawer (stepper, remove, line totals, subtotal, API error display), admin panel (add-product form + inline price/stock/active editing per card).\n- `npm install` + `npm ci` + `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) succeed; dist built from final sources.\n- API test suite `/workspace/.shop_test.py` passes **90/90 \"ALL OK\"** on fresh DB (covers catalog paging/search/sort, auth, cart merge/patch/delete, cross-user isolation, price-from-catalogue, inactive-product exclusion, admin flows/validation,401/403/404 codes).\n- Verified: admin disabled mode (login →401 message), admin re-enabled on restart, data persistence across restarts (alice's cart survived), health `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`, frontend index served at `/`.\n- Dockerfile and README updated for the lock-file install change.\n\n### Active\n- Applying three final refinements just started:\n  1. `frontend/src/components/ProductGrid.tsx`: remove `canAdd` prop so signed-out users can click \"Add to cart\" and get the auth modal (currently `disabled={!canAdd || outOfStock}`); also guard empty price/stock inputs (`Number(\"\") === 0` currently slips through) — was mid-read of the file.\n  2. `frontend/src/App.tsx`: stop passing `canAdd={Boolean(user)}` to `ProductGrid`.\n  3. `backend/app.py`: optionally add simple CORS headers via `after_request` (not yet added).\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Finish ProductGrid edits (drop `canAdd`, add empty-string guards in `save()`), update `App.tsx` usage, optionally add CORS `after_request` hook in `backend/app.py`.\n2. Rebuild frontend (`npm run build`), re-run `/workspace/.shop_test.py` against a fresh server, then cleanup: delete `/workspace/.shop_test.py`, stop gunicorn (`pkill -x gunicorn`), `rm -rf /workspace/data`, restart server fresh to verify seed + health, and review `git status`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: entire Flask API, DB schema/seed/admin init, static serving.\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`, `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: flask 3.1.3 + gunicorn 26.2.0 (lock used as install file).\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`: install step changed to `pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.lock`.\n- `/workspace/README.md`: run contract; lock-file wording updated.\n- `/workspace/frontend/package.json`: adds `tailwindcss@4.3.5`, `@tailwindcss/vite@4.3.5`, `typescript@5.9.3`, `@types/react(-dom)@19.3.0`; build = `tsc --noEmit && vite build`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/vite.config.ts`: `tailwindcss()` plugin + `/api` proxy to `localhost:8000`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json`: strict, noUnusedLocals/Parameters.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx`: main state (user, cart, catalogue, auth/cart modals), all API orchestration.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts`: fetch wrapper, `ApiError` with status, localStorage session keys `shop_token` / `shop_username`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/types.ts`: `Product`, `ProductPage`, `CartItem`, `Cart`, `User`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/components/`: `Header.tsx`, `AuthModal.tsx`, `ProductGrid.tsx`, `CartDrawer.tsx`, `AdminPanel.tsx`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/index.css`: Tailwind entry only.\n- `/workspace/.shop_test.py`: temp API test suite — must be deleted before finishing.","time":{"start":1794381653794,"end":1794381653796}}}
